  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the second of its 6 runs, with all 10 witnesses passing. The first run failed one check because I named the bearing's forward component `\"longitudinal\"`; Core only accepts `\"x\"`/`\"y\"` there, so I changed it to `\"x\"`.\n\n**How the rule reads:**\n- **When it applies:** there is a pedestrian whose pass by the rider is recognised now. At some point between the start of the pass (the last moment the pedestrian was ahead, heading the same way) and now, the rider was on a sidewalk and moving.\n- **What it requires:** at the start of the pass, look back over the stretch where the pedestrian has been ahead. A horn or bell/whistle found there means compliant. If that stretch is seen to begin with no signal, it is violated. If the stretch runs back past the start of the recording, or the signal wasn't observed, the result is unknown.\n\n**One problem you should know about:** the run's reading includes no road-user class under the electric-scooter aggregate (`DEF-LVMC-11-02-083`), and lists `ru.electric_scooter` itself as unresolved. A rider marked only as an electric scooter therefore always has an unknown class. The rule can never find such a rider violated or compliant, only not applicable.\n- `branch_1` is planned as an electric scooter but expects \"violated\", so I built it with an **electric bicycle** instead.\n- `branch_2` (expects not applicable) does use a real scooter.\n- The reading should list `ru.electric_scooter` as included under that aggregate. I've written this up in `task_result.md`.\n\n**Other choices I made:**\n- I left out the record's \"not the subject\" condition. A rider can't overtake itself, so it would never decide anything.\n- I added three witnesses so every condition is exercised:\n  - `branch_3`: the rider is on the sidewalk during the pass only while stopped (not applicable).\n  - `branch_4`: the road user passed is another bicycle (not applicable).\n  - `branch_5`: the horn is used instead of the bell (compliant).\n\nEarly on I mistakenly sent an extra shell command that wrapped the gate call; it was blocked automatically, so nothing ran and no gate run was used.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/fsw/portfolios/av/projects/av_alpamayo_reasoning/users/wcong/WorldModelSpec/.worktrees/full221-v2/pipeline/traffic-spec-agent`:\n- `library/TrafficSpec/Rules/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_40_180_C_o2.lean`\n- `library/TrafficSpecWitness/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_40_180_C_o2.lean`\n- `results/full221-1116-1018/iter-002/code/LVMC_11_40_180_C_o2/task_result.md`",
